From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:49:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/text-input: Drop a pending cursor rectangle when
 focus moves on

A cursor rectangle update waits for the surface's next pre-state-applied
signal before it is passed to the input method, and only connects to it
while no update is pending. When focus left the surface before that,
for example because its window closed, the signal never came and the
handler ID stayed set, so no text input focused afterwards told the
input method where its cursor is.

Disconnect the pending update when focus leaves the surface.
---
 src/wayland/meta-wayland-text-input.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-text-input.c b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-text-input.c
index ef1866aea..2ed8af261 100644
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-text-input.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-text-input.c
@@ -574,6 +574,8 @@ meta_wayland_text_input_set_focus (MetaWaylandTextInput *text_input,
           reset_text_input_focus (text_input);
         }
 
+      g_clear_signal_handler (&text_input->cursor_update.signal_id,
+                              text_input->surface);
       wl_list_remove (&text_input->surface_listener.link);
       text_input->surface = NULL;
       /* Wayland set_surrounding_text() does not support to set null string
